# 01 System Flow Diagram

```mermaid
graph TD
    %% Define Styles
    classDef glass stroke:#00e5ff,stroke-width:2px,fill:#12121a,color:#ffffff
    classDef neon stroke:#9c27b0,stroke-width:2px,fill:#12121a,color:#ffffff

    %% Nodes
    A["🌐 Web Browser (Guest)"]:::glass
    B["💾 LocalStorage (Offline Storage)"]:::glass
    C["🔐 Auth Provider (Login)"]:::neon
    D["🔄 Sync Engine (sync-service.ts)"]:::neon
    E["🏠 PostgreSQL Database (Cloud)"]:::neon

    %% Flow
    A -->|Immediate Read/Write| B
    B -->|Persist Guest Data| B
    A -->|Trigger Login| C
    C -->|Return JWT| D
    B -->|Extract Local Data| D
    D -->|Map Local IDs to UUIDs| D
    D -->|Atomic Batch Sync| E
    E -->|Confirmation| D
    D -->|Clear LocalStorage| B
    A -->|Live Production View| E
```

### Story: The Guest Discovery Phase
The diagram above represents the "Zero Friction" journey. A user lands on FlowShan, interacts with the Kanban board immediately (Guest Phase), and only when they decide to commit, the **Sync Engine** wakes up to bridge their local world to the cloud.
